WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:12.020 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  [Music]  today i'm going to present to you a new  perspective to street photography the 14  millimeter wide angle lens in  combination with my new sony film  simulation the kodak ultra max 400 this  new film simulation has become my number  one choice in every situation over the  past couple months and the results keep  on surprising me  for the past three months i've been  researching testing and working on new  film simulations for sony cameras and  they are finally here  some of these film simulations are the  kodak ultra max 400 porsche 400 fuji  classic chrome and the original  kodachrome 64 and many more  these profiles come together with luts  to get you even closer to the original  film look  you can find both the film profiles and  the luts on my website store links down  below  so before we start if you're excited  about these film profiles hit the like  button subscribe and check the  notification bell to be notified of any  upcoming videos  lately i kept seeing street photography  taken with 85 mil lens but i think  that's lazy photography for a number of  reasons first being that you can keep  your distance from the subject and with  that you don't get out of your comfort  zone  it's much easier to build composition  when you have less background to work  with and also because longer lenses  allow you more time to think and compose  while standing in one place and the last  one is debatable with longer focal  lengths you have more subject background  separation and consequently more bokeh  which enhances the aesthetics of the  image but not necessarily the message  you can easily hide flaws and lack of  vision when you have creamy backgrounds  making the image more visually pleasing  that is not the main focus of street  photography to be only pretty at least  not how i see it for me street  photography is about capturing the  present moment sharing feelings and  finding interesting compositions street  photography being a very demanding area  with very little time to find the moment  compose and take the shot it is indeed  the branch of photography that requires  more skill courage and creativity  because you never know what or if  anything will happen  most street photographers use a 35 or 50  ml lens to capture their moments so by  shooting street with a super wide angle  lens you will increase the difficulty  considerably this is a challenge for  most people even experienced  photographers  [Music]  and this will push your skills to the  limits because of the intensity of the  moment i have to be snappier more  calculated and mindful of the present  moment the adrenaline rush that comes  with it becomes sort of an addiction  [Music]  currently i'm in a mental state of  burnout and generally speaking i feel  very depleted of creative energy but  shooting with the kodak ultra max 400  has made the process so much more  enjoyable  the 14 millimeter brings out a new  intimate perspective in street  photography being so wide the necessity  of getting close to the subject it's a  must in 95 percent of situations  creating a very immersive reality  close subjects looking enormous while  distant objects appearing to be miles  away it is a lens that creates tension  by pushing everything into extremes  [Music]  the 14 millimeter definitely has a  dramatic sense to it and it's all about  the subject in its environment  while a 35 or 50 mil will offer a more  isolated and intimate perspective  a super wide angle lens will tell the  whole story of the subject in direct  relation to the surroundings  [Music]  with the wide-angle lens you need to  plan the shoot seconds before happening  if you don't want to miss it  need to get very close very fast when  taking the shot  and when you do this you are more than a  viewer from outside perceiving the  action happening you are taking part in  the story while also influencing it  [Music]  although some shots seem to be taken  from a distance in most occasions i was  very close to the subject sometimes with  a camera right in their face  the intensity of the moment will build  up courage and experience leading to  more skillful decisions in the future  this can get very intrusive and  uncomfortable for some and you should  expect different reactions from people  i've only started doing street  photography with this 14 millimeter  about two weeks ago but i already see so  many improvements in my photography  compared to my first day  [Music]  in this last part it was raining pretty  hard so i felt discouraged but in the  end i decided to go out and try to find  some compositions  [Music]  as expected there weren't many people on  the street but it was very calming to be  alone in the city and feeling the rain  falling on my skin  [Music]  for these shots i went for a cold  sinister tone to get the same kind of  look all you have to do is set the white  balance under 2 500 kelvin i have a  video on this subject called cine steel  800t recipe and i'll put the link in the  upper right corner of the video for you  to watch  [Music]  [Music]  overall shooting with a 14 millimeter  was definitely a challenge which at  times can get frustrating but hey don't  give up  i really did enjoy shooting street  photography with this lens and now  longer focal lengths seem even easier to  manage  you can find all 18 film simulations for  sony cameras on my website and if you  like them you can buy me a coffee or  make a shop purchase to get even more in  return  don't forget about the luts to get even  closer to the film look  so till next time keep shooting have fun  and let us know in the comments what you  think about the new profiles see ya

